            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0515" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/649: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-13T21:00:00+01:00">December 13, 1932—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—4:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. From Davis. Your 51, December 12, 9 p.m. I have had a thorough and I think a
                    satisfactory talk with Simon and will cable further <pb facs="0516" n="418"
                        xml:id="pg418"/> details thereon tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Riddell, the Canadian delegate, who asked to see me today, told me … that the
                    Canadian Government had not changed its attitude on the Manchurian question and
                    that their attitude was in accord with ours.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
